{
 "format": 1,
 "version": "1.10.0",
 "min_shell": 1,
 "notes": [
  "Inviting friends is easier: an invite link walks them through picking a password, getting their own free Gemini key (one tap pastes it) and adding Vault to their home screen, on Android or iPhone.",
  "iPhones and iPads count as phones now, with the right install steps.",
  "For the person who runs Vault: once the helper is set up on your PC, make invites and see Stats (who joined, who's active, devices, space used) from your phone or Chromebook too. Stats never show what's in anyone's notes.",
  "Typing in Settings is never interrupted when Vault updates in the background.",
  "A Select button at the top of your notes, and Gemini as the default for chats and notes (Claude only if you switch it on)."
 ],
